add('major', 'paper/main.tex', 'whole paper (103 pages: main text pp. 3-52, references pp. 52-56, appendices pp. 57-103)',
 'Too long and too broad for one arXiv paper in learning theory / AIT. The main text is 50 pages with 12 sections and 155 theorem-like environments (100 theorems, propositions, lemmas or corollaries); the outline\'s own target was 38 + 35 pages. Sections 8-10 (computable versions, NN Bayes, summary of Paper 2) are each a separate topic; the NN section is about one third restatement of unverified claims of slides.',
 'main.toc: Sec 1 p.3, 2 p.7, 3 p.12, 4 p.17, 5 p.22, 6 p.28, 7 p.34, 8 p.39, 9 p.43, 10 p.47, 11 p.49, 12 p.50; App A p.57 ... I p.96; app-verification line 173 "The main text (pages 3--52) runs well beyond its target of about 38 pages".',
 'Target <= 30-35 pages of main text. Concretely: drop App I (7 pp) and Table 1; shorten Sec 10 to one paragraph in the Discussion (Paper 2 is cited); merge Secs 8 and 9 into one section "Computable versions and neural networks" of <= 4 pp (move rem:comp:apples, prop:comp:samplers, rem:comp:selection, rem:comp:uniformties, rem:nn:slides, rem:nn:literature, rem:nn:rigorous to the appendix or related work); move sec:learn:curves except cor:learn:perstep to App C; move thm:hist:gf, thm:hist:expected, prop:hist:lhg, prop:hist:inputloss to App D with a one-paragraph summary; move ex:ood:easyhard and ex:ood:hanniexamples to App F. Alternative: publish Sections 8-9 separately.')
