add('major', 'paper/main.tex', 'title footnote (\\thanks) and discussion.tex line 31 (acknowledgements)',
 'arXiv requires that the listed author take full responsibility for the content. The disclosure states that "no human has yet independently checked all of the mathematics". The disclosure is honest and required by the binding note, but posting an AI-produced 100-page mathematics paper that its sole author has not checked invites moderation problems and readers\' distrust.',
 'main.tex line 8 footnote; discussion.tex line 31 "No human has yet independently checked all of the mathematics, and readers should weigh the results accordingly."',
 'Before submission the author should check at least the main theorems (those in the informal main-results list) and the disclosure should then say so: "The author has checked the proofs of Theorems A-D; the remaining proofs were checked by independent AI referees only." Keep the AI-assistance disclosure as required.')
